  "id": "COMPOUND:21094 - PROTEIN:83",
  "verbalization": "The compound in question, (1S,4R,5S,9S,10R,12S)-16-(2-hydroperoxypropan-2-yl)-5,9-dimethyl-13,14-dioxatetracyclo[10.2.2.01,10.04,9]hexadec-15-ene-5-carboxylic acid, is shown to interact with the Glucagon receptor through multiple pathways. It is a known target of several compounds, including Galantamine Hydrobromide Racemic (15 mg), Schisandilactone G, and Oleodaphnone, all of which are linked to the Glucagon receptor. These findings suggest a potential mechanism of action involving the Glucagon receptor, though the exact mode of interaction remains to be elucidated. The compound's ability to target Jurkat cells, a cell line often used in studies of receptor signaling, further supports its involvement in receptor-mediated pathways. The evidence indicates a consistent relationship between the compound and the Glucagon receptor, though the precise mechanism of action and the compound's biological role in receptor signaling require further investigation.",
